m: what you touched, by what it is worth now

c ranks the log as it writes, an address kept once under its newest verb
(`sh/c:/awk -v addr/`): thirty opens today and one last month are one
line, and two c in flight lose one. the change: c appends and knows
nothing else; m reads and ranks, each day a place was touched worth
2^(-days/7), so a habit outranks a burst, and below a floor it is not
offered. back is not memory: c keeps prev per window, and back is
c `{c -}. what is meant is kept: c sets cur only, e and b record through
m, and o, p and lint stay previews. z stays until m has been lived with.
